    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245-a2">

                <pb facs="0523" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg453"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 625.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">W. H. Russell to the
                            American consul.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Millbank Prison, S. W.</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1883-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 19, 1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Michael or Patrick O’Donnell, the prisoner
                    now in my custody under remand from Bow street police court, charged with the
                    murder of J. Carey, states that he is an American citizen, and has papers in the
                    hands of the metropolitan police to prove his citizenship.</p>
                <p>He is most anxious to have a solicitor appointed to undertake his defense, and as
                    he (the prisoner) is unable to write, he has asked me to inform you of the
                    above, and request you to instruct some one to defend him. The prisoner has no
                    friends in England.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>W. H. RUSSELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy Govenor in
                            charge.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
